S.append(HRFlowable(width="100%", thickness=1.4, color=GREEN, spaceBefore=4, spaceAfter=8))
S.append(P("Built on the 2024 rules, canon-first, from the twenty-six sessions and the film. A man, all the way through: no serum, no machine, no gate. What he has is Jeet Kune Do, a 9mm, a ship, a cybernetic eye that sees the past, and the fact that he keeps not dying when he should. The sheet is sized to that: human-peak numbers, and the luck written down where the show put it."))
S.append(P("<b>Design calls.</b> Monk is the body: Jeet Kune Do is the Open Hand with the names filed off, Deflect Attacks is a man who dodges bullets at arm's length, Evasion is the window, Stunning Strike is the punch that ends a fight. Rogue (Assassin) is the Red Dragon: he was a hitman before he was a cowboy, and the syndicate is where the Sneak Attack with a pistol comes from. Lucky is the point: six Luck Points a day is the fall from the cathedral, the monorail, the hospital, and the stairs at the end, and Nine Lives is the once he shouldn't have walked away from and did. Everything on the sheet is a thing a person could do. That's the show's whole argument."))
S.append(P("Snapshot: The Real Folk Blues, level 20 (Monk 14 / Rogue 6)", h2)); S.append(rule())
